  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1109 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThe low will spin off to the east and ridging will build in \nbehind it, dropping rain chances to nearly 0%. On the bright \nside, the weather this weekend looks fantastic with continued\nafternoon highs in the low to mid 80s, low humidity, and overnight\nlows dropping into the low 50s. That's just about cool enough for\na light jacket! Moving into next week, high pressure will \ncontinue to build in, inching the temperatures back up into the \nupper 80s to maybe low 90s for Nashville by Tuesday. By Wednesday,\nthough models are in some disagreement on strength, there is a \ngeneral agreement that another deep low pressure system will\ndevelop and move over the Great Lakes. This will bring rain and \nstorm chances back into the forecast with another dip in \ntemperatures.",
